<Defs>

  <!--
    The road league (docs/design/peoples.md; DESIGN.md "Rimfolk's peoples"; Source/ColonyCouncil/Peoples/): caravan masters,
    carters and waystation keepers who live by the roads between other peoples' towns. Industrial, on the game's outlander
    parent: few towns of their own (settlementGenerationWeight 0.4), many caravans (PeopleExtension.caravanWeight 3: when the
    game sends a trader caravan, theirs is three times as likely as another's), rich and varied stock, guards in plenty. They
    defend their waystations and raid only when the colony has turned them hostile, at the game's own rules (and rarely then:
    raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve 0.35). Listed once among the world's peoples when a world is made, never required.
    Gear from the game's tags and the mods' (their kinds, below): a coat dyed the league's teal on every wayfarer, the
    teal duster in its guards' one kit. When the snow closes the roads a caravan of theirs asks to winter by the colony's
    wall (Rimfolk_Camp_LeagueWinter), and after a stay that went well leaves a waystone at the gate. Their founding (the
    description): Edda Vane, who took nine waymasters' wagons through Harrow Ford under their flags; the Waystone Book.
    What they honour, fear and say is in their template (on their card). Faith (Ideology): a fixed creed of the
    collective and of trade (VE Memes' trader and republic where loaded), the rustic style. Kind of people (Biotech): seven in ten baseliners; hussars on guard,
    genies keeping the books, highmates, dirtmoles, neanderthals, starjacks (Odyssey), boglegs, stoneborn, Vanilla Races
    Expanded's uhlans and androids, Awakened Apes' bonobos at the bargaining table.
  -->

  <FactionDef ParentName="OutlanderFactionBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_League</defName>
    <label>road league</label>
    <description>A league of caravan masters, carters and waystation keepers who live by the roads between other peoples' towns. They keep few towns of their own, only walled waystations where the roads meet, and send their caravans everywhere, well stocked and well guarded.\n\nTheir ways began at Harrow Ford, where the road belonged to whoever had the most rifles. A carter named Edda Vane lost three wagons and a brother there in one summer, and instead of hiring more guns she rode to every waymaster on the road and asked each for one guard and one wagon; the first caravan of the league went through the ford under nine flags, and nobody fired. The league still keeps the Waystone Book, where every fair dealer on the roads is written in good ink and every robber in red, and a word given at a waystone is never broken.\n\nThey talk prices the way other people talk weather, and a wayfarer's highest praise is "good ink." They deal fairly, keep their word and expect the same, and they remember who robbed them. Their towns are run by waymasters, and the league by a warden of the roads.</description>
    <pawnSingular>wayfarer</pawnSingular>
    <pawnsPlural>wayfarers</pawnsPlural>
    <leaderTitle>warden of the roads</leaderTitle>
    <techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
    <basicMemberKind>Rimfolk_League_Wayfarer</basicMemberKind>
    <factionNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_League</factionNameMaker>
    <settlementNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_LeagueTown</settlementNameMaker>
    <factionIconPath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/League</factionIconPath>
    <settlementTexturePath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/LeagueTown</settlementTexturePath>
    <colorSpectrum>
      <li>(0.16, 0.50, 0.54)</li>
      <li>(0.36, 0.74, 0.76)</li>
    </colorSpectrum>
    <hidden>false</hidden>
    <naturalEnemy>false</naturalEnemy>
    <permanentEnemy>false</permanentEnemy>
    <canSiege>false</canSiege>
    <requiredCountAtGameStart>0</requiredCountAtGameStart>
    <startingCountAtWorldCreation>1</startingCountAtWorldCreation>
    <maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>9999</maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>
    <configurationListOrderPriority>15</configurationListOrderPriority>
    <settlementGenerationWeight>0.4</settlementGenerationWeight>
    <raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve Inherit="False">
      <points>
        <li>(0, 0.35)</li>
      </points>
    </raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve>
    <xenotypeSet Inherit="False">
      <xenotypeChances>
        <Hussar MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.04</Hussar>
        <Genie MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.04</Genie>
        <Highmate MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.03</Highmate>
        <Dirtmole MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.02</Dirtmole>
        <Neanderthal MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.02</Neanderthal>
        <Starjack MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.02</Starjack>
        <DV_Bogleg MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,det.boglegs">0.05</DV_Bogleg>
        <Stoneborn MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,det.stoneborn">0.03</Stoneborn>
        <VREH_Uhlan MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,vanillaracesexpanded.hussar">0.02</VREH_Uhlan>
        <VREA_AndroidAwakened MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,vanillaracesexpanded.android">0.02</VREA_AndroidAwakened>
        <Bonobo MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,OnlyMonkey.AwakenedApes">0.02</Bonobo>
      </xenotypeChances>
    </xenotypeSet>
    <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
    <ideoName>The Long Road</ideoName>
    <ideoDescription>The road belongs to everyone who keeps it. A wayfarer pays the toll, keeps the word given at the waystone, and brings the caravan home with every crate it set out with. Whatever is earned on the road is shared at its end, and a debt is carried until it is paid. No one waymaster rules the road: the league is the waymasters together, as it was the day nine of them sent a wagon each through Harrow Ford.</ideoDescription>
    <forcedMemes>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Collectivist</li>
      <li MayRequire="VanillaExpanded.VMemesE">VME_Trader</li>
      <!-- The waymasters together, as at Harrow Ford: Vanilla Ideology Expanded's republic. -->
      <li MayRequire="VanillaExpanded.VMemesE">VME_Republic</li>
    </forcedMemes>
    <structureMemeWeights Inherit="False">
      <Structure_Ideological MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">3</Structure_Ideological>
      <Structure_TheistAbstract MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">1</Structure_TheistAbstract>
    </structureMemeWeights>
    <styles>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Rustic</li>
    </styles>
    <caravanTraderKinds Inherit="False">
      <li>Rimfolk_Caravan_League_Goods</li>
      <li>Rimfolk_Caravan_League_Far</li>
    </caravanTraderKinds>
    <visitorTraderKinds Inherit="False">
      <li>Rimfolk_Visitor_League</li>
    </visitorTraderKinds>
    <baseTraderKinds Inherit="False">
      <li>Rimfolk_Base_League</li>
    </baseTraderKinds>
    <pawnGroupMakers Inherit="False">
      <li>
        <!-- A fight: their guards and outriders, a hired gun or two -->
        <kindDef>Combat</kindDef>
